// The strict project.
//
// CLAUDE.md §9 asks for TypeScript strict mode and no `any` in shared/ and
// server/. The root tsconfig cannot deliver that yet: it also covers the
// inherited WebGL renderer, ~32k lines of upstream code that was never written
// against strict, and turning it on there is phase-0 archaeology rather than
// phase-1 work.
//
// So the rule applies where the new code is. This project is checked by
// `npm run typecheck:strict` alongside the root `tsc --noEmit`; a file has to
// pass both.
//
// Measured when this was added: the whole of shared/ and server/ passes with
// zero errors, the inherited shared/map and shared/pathfinding included. They
// were going to be exempted; they did not need to be. Keep them in — an
// exemption nobody needs is one somebody later mistakes for a warning.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src/shared/**/*",
    "src/server/**/*",
    "tests/server/**/*",
    "tests/shared/**/*"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
